
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">
    <GeneDef>
        <defName>ProjectMomo_Momo</defName>
        <label>Momo</label>
        <description>This woman has inherited the "Inma" of the current Mamono Lord.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Fertile</iconPath>
        <geneClass>ProjectMomo.Gene_Momo</geneClass>
        <displayCategory>Reproduction</displayCategory>
        <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
        <biostatMet>3</biostatMet>
        <enablesNeeds>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Mana</li>
        </enablesNeeds>
        <disablesNeeds>
            <li>ProjectMomo_Essence</li>
        </disablesNeeds>
        <customEffectDescriptions>
            <li>This woman has inherited the "Inma" of the current Mamono Lord.</li>
            <li>Melee strikes inflict tease damage on pawns without this gene, eroding their willpower.</li>
            <li>Her fertility never fades with age.</li>
            <li>The ailments of old age never touch her; ones she already has silently melt away.</li>
        </customEffectDescriptions>
    </GeneDef>

    <!--
        Flight: grants a leap-style "Fly" ability gizmo and makes the pawn count
        as a flying mount in caravans. The CaravanRidingSpeedFactor offset (base
        1.0 + 2.5 = 3.5x) is read by FlightCaravanSpeedPatch, which counts every
        flyer twice: once for herself and once for a passenger riding on her back.
    -->
    <GeneDef>
        <defName>PMM_Gene_Flight</defName>
        <label>flight</label>
        <description>This woman's body bears powerful wings. She can soar across the battlefield at will, and on the world map she flies - strong enough to carry a passenger on her back.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_LongJumpLegs</iconPath>
        <displayCategory>Movement</displayCategory>
        <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
        <biostatMet>-2</biostatMet>
        <abilities>
            <li>PMM_Ability_FlightLeap</li>
        </abilities>
        <statOffsets>
            <CaravanRidingSpeedFactor>2.5</CaravanRidingSpeedFactor>
        </statOffsets>
        <customEffectDescriptions>
            <li>Grants the "Fly" ability: leap through the air to a distant location, soaring over obstacles.</li>
            <li>In a caravan she flies instead of walking, and can airlift one passenger on her back: each flyer counts as two caravan members moving at 350% speed.</li>
        </customEffectDescriptions>
        <descriptionHyperlinks>
            <AbilityDef>PMM_Ability_FlightLeap</AbilityDef>
        </descriptionHyperlinks>
        <!-- Big & Small: draw the wings. Two pieces, both needed:
             1. thingDefSwap -> BS_HumanoidWithWings gives the pawn the winged BODY
                (real BS_Wing parts) and applies B&S's BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race
                tracker hediff. The tracker is the ONLY wing renderer we use.
             2. The Flagger un-blanks that tracker: it hides its wing graphics on
                pawns carrying a gene tagged Wing/Wings (it expects the separate
                BigSmall_Genes mod to draw them). Raising ShowBaseWingsRight/Left
                tells the tracker to keep drawing its own feathered wings - the
                same trick PMM_Gene_LamiaTail uses with ShowBaseAbdomen.
             We deliberately ship NO custom render hediff: the tracker alone draws
             the wings (confirmed in-game), and a second renderer would just draw
             the same textures twice.
             exclusionTags keep it from stacking with other wing swaps. -->
        <exclusionTags>
            <li>Wings</li>
        </exclusionTags>
        <modExtensions>
            <li Class="BigAndSmall.PawnExtension">
                <!-- forceThingDefSwap: the cautious (non-forced) swap silently
                     refused on dragons - no BS_Wing parts, no tracker, no wings.
                     The lamia tail gets away with cautious because lamias start
                     plain. Dragons need the forced path. -->
                <forceThingDefSwap>true</forceThingDefSwap>
                <!-- renderCacheOff: same as the lamia tail. Wings reach past the
                     body render atlas; without this they get cropped. -->
                <renderCacheOff>true</renderCacheOff>
                <thingDefSwap>BS_HumanoidWithWings</thingDefSwap>
                <!-- Toughen the swapped-in wing parts through the shared hidden
                     hediff (Defs/HediffDefs_BSDurability.xml): wings use the
                     pawn's own HealthScale, which for small races is low - this
                     keeps BS-added parts on the same plumbing as insect chitin. -->
                <applyPartHediff>
                    <li>
                        <hediff>PMM_Hediff_PartToughness</hediff>
                        <bodyparts>
                            <li>BS_Wing</li>
                        </bodyparts>
                    </li>
                </applyPartHediff>
            </li>
            <!-- Keep the B&S race tracker from hiding its wing graphics on the
                 gene path. Same pattern as the lamia tail's ShowBaseAbdomen. -->
            <li Class="BigAndSmall.Flagger">
                <flags>
                    <ShowBaseWingsRight />
                    <ShowBaseWingsLeft />
                </flags>
            </li>
        </modExtensions>
    </GeneDef>

    <!--
        Momo venom: melee strikes inject a slowing toxin into ANY living victim
        (humans, animals and other momos alike). VenomDamagePatch applies the
        build-up (ProjectMomo_VenomBuildup); the hediff only suppresses the
        Moving capacity, so it pins victims down without ever killing them, and
        a full dose wears off in 4 hours. Balance in the Genes settings tab.
    -->
    <GeneDef>
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MomoVenom</defName>
        <label>momo venom</label>
        <description>This momo's body produces a slowing venom that her strikes pass into her victims. As it builds, limbs grow heavy until the victim can no longer stand - helpless, unharmed, and fully conscious. The venom is never lethal and wears off completely within hours.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_PartialToxicityResistance</iconPath>
        <displayCategory>Violence</displayCategory>
        <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
        <customEffectDescriptions>
            <li>Melee strikes inject venom into any living victim - humans, animals and other momos alike.</li>
            <li>The venom slows the victim as it builds (about 20 strikes to fully pin), then wears off completely within 4 hours.</li>
            <li>Non-lethal: a fully envenomed victim simply collapses, conscious and alive.</li>
        </customEffectDescriptions>
    </GeneDef>

    <!--
        Fiery momo: total immunity to fire, heat and lava. Flammability x0
        means vanilla fire-attach always refuses (she can never ignite);
        FireImmunityPatch nullifies every Heat armour-category damage; the
        +1000C comfy-temperature ceiling means no environment can overheat
        her. Men bonded (tsugai) to her gain the lesser ProjectMomo_FieryBondWard
        hediff via FireWardComponent: +40C comfy ceiling, x0.85 flammability,
        x0.85 flame damage.
    -->
    <GeneDef>
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MomoFiery</defName>
        <label>fiery momo</label>
        <description>These momo are unaffected by heat, fire or lava, being infused with an excess of the Fire Element. Typically these momo can control the Fire Element in other ways too.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_FireResistant</iconPath>
        <displayCategory>Temperature</displayCategory>
        <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
        <biostatMet>-4</biostatMet>
        <statFactors>
            <Flammability>0</Flammability>
        </statFactors>
        <statOffsets>
            <ComfyTemperatureMax>1000</ComfyTemperatureMax>
        </statOffsets>
        <customEffectDescriptions>
            <li>Immune to fire, heat and lava: she cannot be set aflame, takes no flame damage, and no heat can discomfort her.</li>
            <li>A man bonded to her shares a lesser ward: +40C max comfortable temperature, 15% less flammable, 15% less flame damage.</li>
        </customEffectDescriptions>
    </GeneDef>

    <!--
        Momo claws: +15% tease damage (MomoClaws.TeaseDealtMultiplier, folded
        into both tease paths), paid for with -15% manipulation
        (ClawsManipulationPatch). The cutting/inflaming flavour is lore only:
        on humanlikes the tease system already replaces wounds entirely.
        Balance in the Genes settings tab.
    -->
    <GeneDef>
        <defName>ProjectMomo_MomoClaws</defName>
        <label>momo claws</label>
        <description>These sharp claws, meant for vicious killing during the time of the last Mamono Lord, now serve a different, more lustful purpose. Momo claws cut the skin, causing a great heat to radiate into the victim's body, inflaming their lusts. These claws however do interfere with the dexterity of the momo.</description>
        <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_StrongMeleeDamage</iconPath>
        <displayCategory>Violence</displayCategory>
        <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
        <customEffectDescriptions>
            <li>Tease damage dealt +15%.</li>
            <li>Manipulation -15%.</li>
        </customEffectDescriptions>
    </GeneDef>
</Defs>
